{"id":21044,"artist":"Nirvana","title":"LAKE OF FIRE","lyrics_plain":"Where do bad folks go when they die?\nThey don't go to Heaven where the angels fly\nThey go to the lake of fire and fry\nSee 'em again 'til the fourth of July!\n\nI knew a lady who came from Duluth\nBit by a dog with a rabid tooth\nShe went to her grave just a little too soon\nFlew away howling on the yellow moon\n\nWhere do bad folks go when they die?\nThey don't go to Heaven where the angels fly\nThey go down to the lake of fire and fry\nSee 'em again 'til the fourth of July\n\nPeople cry and people moan\nLook for a dry place to call their home\nTry to find some place to rest their bones\nWhile the angels and the devils try to make them their own\n\nWhere do bad folks go when they die?\nThey don't go to Heaven where the angels fly\nThey go down to the lake of fire and fry\nSee 'em again 'til the fourth of July","lyrics_synced":"[00:19.66] Where do bad folks go when they die?\n[00:21.90] They don't go to heaven where the angels fly\n[00:24.66] They go down to the lake of fire and fry\n[00:27.59] Won't see them again till the fourth of July\n[00:35.86] I knew a lady who came from Duluth\n[00:38.62] She got bit by a dog with a rabid tooth\n[00:41.38] She went to her grave just a little too soon\n[00:43.45] And she flew away howling on the yellow moon\n[00:47.24] Where do bad folks go when they die?\n[00:49.48] They don't go to heaven where the angels fly\n[00:52.24] They go down to the lake of fire and fry\n[00:55.17] Won't see them again till the fourth of July\n[01:03.10] Now the people cry\n[01:04.31] And the people moan\n[01:06.21] And they look for a dry place\n[01:07.59] To call their home\n[01:08.97] And try to find some place to rest their bones\n[01:11.38] While the angels and the devils\n[01:12.76] Fight to claim them for their own\n[01:14.83] Where do bad folks go when they die?\n[01:17.07] They don't go to heaven where the angels fly\n[01:19.83] They go down to the lake of fire and fry\